WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.353
Work from Home.

2
00:00:01.633 --> 00:00:05.793
Day 74 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Workplace phase.

3
00:00:07.543 --> 00:00:08.567
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.847 --> 00:00:13.028
When you work from home, people judge you by your output and your communication.

5
00:00:13.308 --> 00:00:15.207
Nobody sees how hard you're working.

6
00:00:15.487 --> 00:00:20.308
Be easy to reach, visible, and reliable, and still switch off at the end of the day.

7
00:00:21.658 --> 00:00:22.511
Part 1.

8
00:00:22.791 --> 00:00:24.306
The remote trust formula.

9
00:00:25.556 --> 00:00:29.268
Responsive: reply within an agreed time during working hours.

10
00:00:29.548 --> 00:00:32.769
Visible: progress shared in writing, without being asked.

11
00:00:33.049 --> 00:00:35.183
Reliable: do what you said, when you said.

12
00:00:35.463 --> 00:00:39.239
Present: camera on, engaged in meetings, not multitasking.

13
00:00:39.519 --> 00:00:42.121
Sustainable: clear start and end to the day.

14
00:00:43.471 --> 00:00:44.346
Part 2.

15
00:00:44.626 --> 00:00:46.119
Asking for work from home.

16
00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:49.204
Occasional WFH day.

17
00:00:49.484 --> 00:00:50.423
You could say:

18
00:00:50.703 --> 00:00:52.623
I'd like to work from home on Thursday.

19
00:00:52.903 --> 00:00:54.801
I have a plumber coming in the morning.

20
00:00:55.081 --> 00:00:59.881
I'll be online for the stand-up and all my meetings, and reachable on Slack all day.

21
00:01:01.231 --> 00:01:03.663
Regular hybrid or remote arrangement.

22
00:01:03.943 --> 00:01:04.882
You could say:

23
00:01:05.162 --> 00:01:08.447
I'd like to propose working from home on Mondays and Fridays.

24
00:01:08.727 --> 00:01:12.802
My commute is 3 hours a day, and I'd use that time for focused work.

25
00:01:13.082 --> 00:01:15.023
I suggest we try it for 2 months:

26
00:01:15.303 --> 00:01:21.618
I'll keep my core hours at 10 to 6, join every meeting on video, and send a short update each Friday.

27
00:01:21.898 --> 00:01:23.711
Then we review whether it's working.

28
00:01:25.061 --> 00:01:29.904
Lead with what the company gets, offer a trial period, and suggest how you'll measure it.

29
00:01:31.254 --> 00:01:33.729
Temporary (health, family, relocation).

30
00:01:34.009 --> 00:01:34.947
You could say:

31
00:01:35.227 --> 00:01:39.921
My father has surgery next month, and I'll need to be in Lucknow for about 3 weeks.

32
00:01:40.201 --> 00:01:42.313
Could I work remotely during that time?

33
00:01:42.593 --> 00:01:44.790
I'll keep my usual hours and meetings.

34
00:01:45.070 --> 00:01:48.633
If there are a couple of days I need off, I'll take leave for those.

35
00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:51.241
Request turned down.

36
00:01:51.521 --> 00:01:52.460
You could say:

37
00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:53.807
I understand.

38
00:01:54.087 --> 00:01:56.049
Could you help me understand the concern?

39
00:01:56.329 --> 00:02:04.052
If it's about availability or collaboration, I'd be happy to try a shorter trial, or one day a week, so we can see how it goes.

40
00:02:05.402 --> 00:02:06.298
Part 3.

41
00:02:06.578 --> 00:02:08.413
Daily communication from home.

42
00:02:09.663 --> 00:02:11.476
Start and end your day visibly.

43
00:02:11.756 --> 00:02:13.633
Here is a template you can copy.

44
00:02:13.913 --> 00:02:15.300
Morning (team channel).

45
00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.497
Good morning!

46
00:02:16.777 --> 00:02:21.428
Today: finishing slot-booking API tests, then PR review for Meena.

47
00:02:21.708 --> 00:02:24.993
Available all day except 2 to 3 pm (doctor).

48
00:02:25.273 --> 00:02:26.191
End of day.

49
00:02:26.471 --> 00:02:27.431
Logging off.

50
00:02:27.711 --> 00:02:31.017
Done: slot API tests, Meena's PR reviewed.

51
00:02:31.297 --> 00:02:33.196
Tomorrow: integrate with the cart.

52
00:02:33.476 --> 00:02:34.564
No blockers.

53
00:02:37.414 --> 00:02:38.694
Status and presence.

54
00:02:38.974 --> 00:02:40.318
Here is a quick table:

55
00:02:40.598 --> 00:02:42.091
Status, and Use it for.

56
00:02:42.371 --> 00:02:43.182
Active:

57
00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:44.742
Working, reachable.

58
00:02:45.022 --> 00:02:46.494
Focus or heads-down:

59
00:02:46.774 --> 00:02:48.374
Deep work till 1 pm.

60
00:02:48.654 --> 00:02:49.870
Ping me if urgent.

61
00:02:50.150 --> 00:02:51.217
Lunch or away:

62
00:02:51.497 --> 00:02:52.457
Back at 2.

63
00:02:52.737 --> 00:02:53.355
Off:

64
00:02:53.635 --> 00:02:55.043
Outside working hours.

65
00:02:56.393 --> 00:02:57.033
Tip:

66
00:02:57.313 --> 00:02:58.892
The response-time agreement.

67
00:02:59.172 --> 00:03:06.340
Agree with your team: for example, Slack within ~1 hour, email within a day, phone call for real emergencies.

68
00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:09.521
That frees everyone from having to watch Slack all day.

69
00:03:10.871 --> 00:03:11.789
Part 4.

70
00:03:12.069 --> 00:03:13.477
Video calls from home.

71
00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:19.569
Camera on for one-on-ones and small meetings; at eye level, face lit from the front.

72
00:03:19.849 --> 00:03:22.068
Neutral background or a simple blur.

73
00:03:22.348 --> 00:03:26.572
Headset with a mic (laptop mics pick up the pressure cooker and the doorbell).

74
00:03:26.852 --> 00:03:29.455
Mute when not speaking; unmute before talking.

75
00:03:29.735 --> 00:03:33.447
Test audio or screen share 2 minutes before important calls.

76
00:03:33.727 --> 00:03:37.097
Close other tabs and notifications before screen sharing.

77
00:03:38.447 --> 00:03:40.389
Home interruptions: what to say.

78
00:03:40.669 --> 00:03:42.013
Here is a quick table:

79
00:03:42.293 --> 00:03:43.679
Situation, and Say.

80
00:03:43.959 --> 00:03:45.111
Background noise:

81
00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.439
Sorry, there's some construction noise.

82
00:03:47.719 --> 00:03:49.767
I'll stay on mute when I'm not speaking.

83
00:03:50.047 --> 00:03:51.477
Family member walks in:

84
00:03:51.757 --> 00:03:53.399
(Smile) Sorry, one moment.

85
00:03:53.679 --> 00:03:55.237
Mute, handle it, return:

86
00:03:55.517 --> 00:03:57.010
Sorry about that, I'm back.

87
00:03:57.290 --> 00:03:58.378
Internet drops:

88
00:03:58.658 --> 00:04:01.837
(Chat or phone) Lost connection, rejoining in 2 minutes.

89
00:04:02.117 --> 00:04:02.927
After:

90
00:04:03.207 --> 00:04:05.213
Sorry, what was the last point I missed?

91
00:04:05.493 --> 00:04:06.453
Power cut:

92
00:04:06.733 --> 00:04:07.863
Message the team:

93
00:04:08.143 --> 00:04:10.149
Power cut here, on mobile data.

94
00:04:10.429 --> 00:04:11.794
Joining audio-only.

95
00:04:12.074 --> 00:04:13.269
Need to step away:

96
00:04:13.549 --> 00:04:15.469
I need to step away for 10 minutes.

97
00:04:15.749 --> 00:04:17.199
I'll catch up from the notes.

98
00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:19.509
Part 5.

99
00:04:19.789 --> 00:04:22.029
Staying visible when you're not in the office.

100
00:04:23.279 --> 00:04:27.482
Write down your work: design docs, PR descriptions, weekly updates.

101
00:04:27.762 --> 00:04:31.133
In a remote team, written work is how people see what you do.

102
00:04:31.413 --> 00:04:32.543
Speak in meetings.

103
00:04:32.823 --> 00:04:36.877
Remote people are easy to forget; contribute in the first 5 minutes.

104
00:04:37.157 --> 00:04:41.317
Use the chat in meetings to add links, ideas, and +1, agree.

105
00:04:41.597 --> 00:04:43.069
Do virtual coffee chats:

106
00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:46.762
15 minutes, camera on, no agenda, 1 to 2 per week.

107
00:04:47.042 --> 00:04:49.538
Celebrate others publicly in team channels.

108
00:04:50.888 --> 00:04:55.688
Turn up in person for planning days, team events and big launches, if you're hybrid.

109
00:04:57.038 --> 00:04:57.977
Part 6.

110
00:04:58.257 --> 00:04:59.921
Writing well for remote work.

111
00:05:01.171 --> 00:05:02.515
Here is a quick table:

112
00:05:02.795 --> 00:05:03.989
Unclear, and Clear.

113
00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:05.016
Hi...

114
00:05:05.296 --> 00:05:06.107
(waits):

115
00:05:06.387 --> 00:05:08.776
One complete message with the full question.

116
00:05:09.056 --> 00:05:10.080
Can we connect?:

117
00:05:10.360 --> 00:05:14.499
Can we do a 15-min call today about the slot API contract?

118
00:05:14.779 --> 00:05:16.315
Free 3 to 5 pm.

119
00:05:16.595 --> 00:05:17.277
Done?:

120
00:05:17.557 --> 00:05:19.157
Is the payment PR merged?

121
00:05:19.437 --> 00:05:21.272
I need it to start the refund work.

122
00:05:21.552 --> 00:05:22.619
Long paragraph:

123
00:05:22.899 --> 00:05:25.992
Bullet points, the ask in bold, a deadline with a time.

124
00:05:27.342 --> 00:05:33.593
See Day-to-Day Communication and Global and Remote Teams for message templates and time-zone tips.

125
00:05:34.943 --> 00:05:35.881
Part 7.

126
00:05:36.161 --> 00:05:37.292
Boundaries at home.

127
00:05:38.542 --> 00:05:43.897
Fixed start and end times, with a short commute ritual (walk, tea) to start and end the day.

128
00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:47.505
Separate workspace where possible, even a corner of a room.

129
00:05:47.785 --> 00:05:49.854
Real lunch break away from the screen.

130
00:05:50.134 --> 00:05:53.291
Notifications off after hours (except on-call).

131
00:05:53.571 --> 00:05:55.150
Tell your family your schedule:

132
00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:57.969
Meetings 11 to 1, please knock first.

133
00:05:59.319 --> 00:06:00.257
You could say:

134
00:06:00.537 --> 00:06:07.535
(To a manager who messages late) I log off at 7 to spend time with family, so I'll reply first thing in the morning.

135
00:06:07.815 --> 00:06:11.036
For production issues, the on-call number works any time.

136
00:06:12.386 --> 00:06:14.349
More scripts in Leave and Boundaries.

137
00:06:15.699 --> 00:06:16.573
Part 8.

138
00:06:16.853 --> 00:06:18.261
Feeling isolated?

139
00:06:19.511 --> 00:06:21.943
Pair-program on video for a few hours a week.

140
00:06:22.223 --> 00:06:25.722
Join or start a non-work channel (cricket, cooking, pets).

141
00:06:26.002 --> 00:06:28.967
Work from a café or co-working space once a week.

142
00:06:29.247 --> 00:06:30.357
Tell your manager.

143
00:06:30.637 --> 00:06:33.943
Isolation affects performance, and a good lead will help.

144
00:06:35.293 --> 00:06:36.189
Part 9.

145
00:06:36.469 --> 00:06:38.411
For leads managing remote teams.

146
00:06:39.661 --> 00:06:41.965
Judge outcomes, not online status.

147
00:06:42.245 --> 00:06:45.658
Hold regular one-on-ones on video; ask How are you, really?

148
00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:51.613
Run meetings remote-first: if one person is remote, everyone joins from their laptop.

149
00:06:51.893 --> 00:06:56.330
Write decisions down so remote people aren't left out of hallway conversations.

150
00:06:56.610 --> 00:07:01.197
Watch for silent struggle: remote people often hide being blocked or burned out.

151
00:07:02.547 --> 00:07:03.400
Part 10.

152
00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:05.067
Practice conversation:

153
00:07:05.347 --> 00:07:06.840
Proposing hybrid work.

154
00:07:08.090 --> 00:07:10.117
Here is how the conversation goes.

155
00:07:10.397 --> 00:07:14.386
I'd like to propose working from home on Mondays and Fridays.

156
00:07:14.666 --> 00:07:15.839
What's the reason?

157
00:07:16.119 --> 00:07:18.210
My commute is three hours a day.

158
00:07:18.490 --> 00:07:20.986
I'd use that time for focused work.

159
00:07:21.266 --> 00:07:23.634
My worry is that you'll miss team discussions.

160
00:07:23.914 --> 00:07:25.279
I understand.

161
00:07:25.559 --> 00:07:32.194
I'll keep core hours from 10 to 6, join every meeting on camera, and come in for planning days.

162
00:07:33.544 --> 00:07:35.144
The conversation continues.

163
00:07:35.424 --> 00:07:36.533
Okay.

164
00:07:36.813 --> 00:07:39.117
Let's try it for two months and then review.

165
00:07:39.397 --> 00:07:40.336
Thank you.

166
00:07:40.616 --> 00:07:45.053
I'll send a short update every Friday so we can see how it's going.

167
00:07:46.403 --> 00:07:47.939
That's the end of this lesson.

168
00:07:48.219 --> 00:07:52.870
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

169
00:07:53.150 --> 00:07:59.273
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

